WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:01.913
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.913 --> 00:00:06.170
- Oh, my goodness, I played, I
guess you might say, forever.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:10.603
Probably about 1931 is
when I first started.

00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:12.329
It'd be 85 years approximately

00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:14.598
that I've been playin' hockey.

00:00:14.598 --> 00:00:16.511
I'm Mark Sertich.

00:00:16.511 --> 00:00:20.164
I'm the oldest ice hockey
player in the world.

00:00:20.164 --> 00:00:22.897
(uptempo, rhythmic music)

00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:26.647
I'm 95 years old, hope
to be 96 on July 18th.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.328
I'm still playin' hockey
three times a week.

00:00:32.328 --> 00:00:34.173
I get up at 6:00 in the morning,

00:00:34.173 --> 00:00:38.178
I do my sit ups, my push
ups and a few other things

00:00:38.178 --> 00:00:42.345
that kinda loosen me up and
then I'm ready to go, yeah.

00:00:43.335 --> 00:00:45.936
(uptempo, rhythmic music)

00:00:45.936 --> 00:00:47.358
I only live about a mile away,

00:00:47.358 --> 00:00:50.330
but I do drive down by
myself and it's funny,

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.913
but I'm usually the last one there

00:00:51.913 --> 00:00:56.080
and I'm the one that lives
the closest (laughing).

00:00:57.171 --> 00:01:01.366
The group consists mostly
of some former firefighters

00:01:01.366 --> 00:01:03.500
and also, of course, the current ones,

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.920
so there's quite a
different mixture there.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.825
I think about my age and once in a while

00:01:09.825 --> 00:01:11.499
I say to myself, “Well, you know

00:01:11.499 --> 00:01:13.436
you're only 59, you're not 95.”

00:01:13.436 --> 00:01:18.339
I just turn the numbers around
to make myself feel better.

00:01:18.339 --> 00:01:21.696
My love for hockey is hard to explain.

00:01:21.696 --> 00:01:24.197
You're skatin' with the puck,
you're shootin' the puck,

00:01:24.197 --> 00:01:26.432
you're tryin' to take the
puck away from the other guy,

00:01:26.432 --> 00:01:27.857
there are so many different
things you're doin'

00:01:27.857 --> 00:01:30.690
that it just keeps ya goin' there.

00:01:31.773 --> 00:01:33.123
- Everybody's got a role.

00:01:33.123 --> 00:01:37.290
I'll keep dishin' to you and
you just keep finishing it.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:39.927
- Yeah, I'll try.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.249
If the coach keeps puttin' us out there,

00:01:42.249 --> 00:01:44.384
we're doin' somethin' right.

00:01:44.384 --> 00:01:47.134
(dramatic music)

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:54.913
They're the greatest bunch of
guys I've ever played with.

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:56.660
They set me up all the time

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.721
and sometimes it gets to a point

00:01:58.721 --> 00:02:01.493
where I'm almost embarrassed
that I'm not scoring more

00:02:01.493 --> 00:02:06.039
because they're always givin'
me the puck (laughing).

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:08.603
A group of the players,
right after hockey,

00:02:08.603 --> 00:02:12.402
they'll come over to my home
and we sit down in the kitchen

00:02:12.402 --> 00:02:16.569
and discuss who did what on
the ice and so on and so forth.

00:02:18.359 --> 00:02:20.627
At my age, it's a wonderful way

00:02:20.627 --> 00:02:22.689
of bein' connected with younger people,

00:02:22.689 --> 00:02:26.802
and I think that's very
important for an older person.

00:02:26.802 --> 00:02:31.025
I'm so fortunate that it gives
me a chance to be involved.

00:02:31.025 --> 00:02:35.192
It's really the best thing
that's every happened to me.

